  "abstract": {
    "value": "The synthesis of allenic acids and esters and their conversion to butenolides has been examined in some detail. Racemic butenolides 10 are efficiently prepared from the esters 8 through treatment with $\\mathbf { B C l _ { 3 } }$ and exposure of the derived acid 9 to catalytic ${ \\bf A g N O _ { 3 } }$ in acetone. Conversion of the enantioenriched allenylstannane (S)-17 to the acid 18 through lithiation and subsequent carboxylation with $\\mathbf { C O _ { 2 } }$ afforded racemic product. The enantioenriched propargylic mesylates 16 and 22 afforded the allenic esters 19 and 23 with inversion of configuration through treatment with $\\mathrm { P d } ( \\mathrm { P h } _ { 3 } \\mathrm { P } ) _ { 4 }$, CO, and the appropriate alcohol in THF. These reactions proceeded with ca. 10% or less of racemization. The allenic esters 23 yielded the iodobutenolides 24 by reaction with IBr. Hydrogenolysis to the butenolide 25 was achieved with Pd(PPh3)4 and $\\mathbf { B u _ { 3 } S n H }.$. Alternatively, the allenic acids 27 could be prepared directly from mesylates 22 with $\\mathbf { P d } ( \\mathbf { P P h } _ { 3 } ) _ { 4 }$ and CO in aqueous THF. Cyclization to the butenolides 25 was achieved, as before, with catalytic ${ \\bf A g N O _ { 3 } }$.",
    "source": "content_list_first_paragraph_after_authors",
    "confidence": 0.68,
    "human_checked": false
  },
